      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the area of a square with a given perimeter, we first need to understand the relationship between the perimeter and the side length of the square. \n\nThe perimeter \\( P \\) of a square is given by the formula:\n\\[ P = 4s \\]\nwhere \\( s \\) is the length of one side of the square. \n\nWe are given that the perimeter \\( P \\) is 32 feet. Therefore, we can set up the equation:\n\\[ 4s = 32 \\]\n\nTo find the side length \\( s \\), we solve for \\( s \\) by dividing both sides of the equation by 4:\n\\[ s = \\frac{32}{4} = 8 \\]\nSo, the side length of the square is 8 feet.\n\nThe area \\( A \\) of a square is given by the formula:\n\\[ A = s^2 \\]\nSubstituting the side length \\( s = 8 \\) feet into the formula, we get:\n\\[ A = 8^2 = 64 \\]\nTherefore, the area of the square is:\n\\[ \\boxed{64} \\]\n\nHere is a step-by-step summary:\n1. Find the side length of the square using the perimeter.\n2. Calculate the area of the square using the side length.\n\nThe area of the square is \\(\\boxed{64}\\) square feet.",
